{"availability":"available","full":"veodyn/veodyn-ce","name":"veodyn-ce","description":"Veodyn community edition: the data substrate for regional transportation hubs and agencies.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":16,"forks":1,"created":"2026-08-11T21:56:19Z","updated":"2026-10-04T13:17:54Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://demo.veodyn.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T16:29:44.149Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T16:29:44.149Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T16:29:44.149Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:36.103Z","stars":16,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:44.149Z","stars":16,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["One source of truth for a region's transportation operations. Veodyn pulls from the systems an agency already runs, normalizes what arrives, stores it locally, serves it over an API, and draws it. This repository is the community node: open source, self-hosted, and complete on its own.","Website · Documentation · Live demo · Getting started · Connectors · Editions","More captures of every screen are in docs/static/img/screenshots/, and the documentation walks through each one."],"features":["Connectors for the sources an agency already runs: GTFS-Realtime, static","Historical capture of any feed into ClickHouse on a cadence you declare,","Queries: a SQL editor with a schema browser, parameters, schedules,","Visualizations: 15 core types (table, chart, counter, pivot, funnel, map,","Dashboards: results on a drag-and-drop grid, with auto-refresh,"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/veodyn/veodyn-ce/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"992016932069f1e01e044e238b68ba147e4995a00ed1b76d95fe0274e605b8f1","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:36.364Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:55:53.873Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"One source of truth for a region's transportation operations. Veodyn pulls from the systems an agency already runs, normalizes what arrives, stores it locally, serves it over an API, and draws it. This repository is the community node: open source, self-hosted, and complete on its own.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/veodyn/veodyn-ce/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"This repository is the community node: open source, self-hosted, and complete on its own.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/veodyn/veodyn-ce/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Pick one of the demo personas on the sign-in page; the demo accounts are shared and reset regularly.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/veodyn/veodyn-ce/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"and webhook destinations, password and Google sign-in.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/veodyn/veodyn-ce/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"That is the whole install. compose.yaml at the repository root builds all three services and bootstraps itself: it creates both databases, runs both migration sets (the query service's own schema creation and the sidecar's Alembic revisions), generates its own cookie secret and API keys into a volume, seeds a query-service admin plus a separate non-admin service account for…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/veodyn/veodyn-ce/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Then it waits for each healthcheck, asserts all three bootstrap containers exited 0, asserts the frontend, the query service and the sidecar answer on /api/healthcheck, /ping and /health, checks the sidecar's schema is at its head revision, verifies both seeded API keys, and signs the admin in through the frontend's own login route.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/veodyn/veodyn-ce/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"992016932069f1e01e044e238b68ba147e4995a00ed1b76d95fe0274e605b8f1","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/veodyn/veodyn-ce/blob/ma